## Summary
A collection of 5,000 classic movie posters from various film eras has been digitized and made available online for free browsing and downloading. The collection includes works from designers like Saul Bass and spans genres such as 70s kitsch, grindhouse films, and silent avant-garde cinema, preserving cinematic art history.

## Key Points
- 5,000 classic movie posters have been digitized and put online.
- The posters are freely accessible for browsing and downloading.
- The collection features diverse film styles and eras, including Saul Bass designs, 70s kitsch, grindhouse, and silent avant-garde.
- This project promotes public access to historical cinematic art.


